('apps.fontforge','font')` ('menu keeps a better-matching menu entry above a weaker app match'). It now asserts the reverse. The proof-side copy at menumodel-replay.test.mjs:413 is inverted the same way, outside any test() block. review.compat test_diff reports '2 existing test file(s) changed' and flags neither inversion, so no compat approval gate covers this retired guarantee. The PR states the inversion verbatim (\"replaces the previous guarantee ... (`style.font` vs `apps.fontforge` for `font`)\"). It is intended, but a human reviewer should approve it as explicitly as cf-6ea9f79aa0b1c1de. This is my reading of the diff; the engine has no record for it (the typed claim only checks that menu-test.sh is on SJ7P's changed files).","refs":[{"id":"test/shell.d/menu-test.sh","kind":"file","line":473},{"id":"test/node/menumodel-replay.test.mjs","kind":"file","line":413},{"id":"SW-REQ-260922-SJ7P","kind":"requirement"}],"severity":"medium","title":"Upstream inverted an existing assertion in test/shell.d/menu-test.sh; no compat finding records it","verification":{"evidence":[{"id":"SW-REQ-260922-SJ7P","kind":"requirement"}],"method":"review.changes (spec, code-trace, function and call-level requirement impact)","note":"SW-REQ-260922-SJ7P is in review.changes (modified, matchLevel function).","status":"confirmed"}},{"detail":"review.behaviorDiff ran 213 inputs over 5 partitions (corpus 17, data 176, lifecycle 14, scale 3, timing 3) with 0 differences. test/bdiff/harness.mjs drives JSONC parsing and the menu request lifecycle, and stubs rebuildDisplay with fixed rows (harness.mjs:252). Neither path calls searchScore with a query, so the result says nothing about ranking. I ran base 58cd8018 vs head d29af2a6 rebuildDisplay under node vm with the shipped menu (scratch only). For vsc, base gives `setup.default.editor.vscode, install.editor.vscode, apps.code` and head gives `apps.code | ...`. For system, `system | apps.btop` becomes `apps.btop | system`. Root tu without apps is identical. These results are outside the package, so no behavior_changed claim can be typed.","refs":[{"id":"test/bdiff/harness.mjs","kind":"file","line":252},{"id":"shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml","kind":"file","line":711}],"severity":"medium","title":"Opinion (my own run, not engine-verified): the differential found no difference, but its harness does not exercise search ranking","verification":{"evidence":[],"method":"untyped finding","note":"No typed claim: this finding is the author's judgement and is not checked against the package.","status":"unverifiable"}},{"claim":{"params":{"relatesTo":["shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml:rebuildDisplay","shell/plugins/menu/MenuModel.js:searchScore"],"scenario":"root search for 'system' with btop installed (GenericName System Monitor, Keywords system): Enter runs apps.btop instead of the exact-label System menu"},"type":"behavior_hazard"},"detail":"At d29af2a6 with the shipped default menu, a root search for `system` puts apps.btop (aliases system/process/task) above the menu entry labelled exactly System. Enter then opens btop. The bias decides this, and the pinning in rebuildDisplay reinforces it. The PR discloses the general tradeoff but not the exact-label case. The mirror's witness pins only the description-only form ('update', menumodel-replay.test.mjs:1425). A maintainer decision is needed.","refs":[{"id":"shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml","kind":"file","line":711},{"id":"shell/plugins/menu/MenuModel.js","kind":"file","line":377},{"id":"SW-REQ-260922-SJ7P","kind":"requirement"},{"id":"SW-REQ-260922-TKDP","kind":"requirement"}],"severity":"medium","title":"Question: should a keyword-only app match beat an exact-label menu entry?","verification":{"evidence":[],"method":"behavior hazard: settled only by a recorded test outcome","note":"A runtime-behavior question the package's static facts cannot settle; it needs a test. Suggested test: \"Exact-label menu entry vs keyword-only app\".","status":"needs_test"}},{"claim":{"params":{"relatesTo":["shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml:rebuildDisplay"],"scenario":"root search 'tu' with one installed app matching: the divider between direct children (setup) and deeper entries (install.tui) is no longer drawn"},"type":"behavior_hazard"},"detail":"For root `tu`, base gives `setup | install.tui ... apps.code ...` and head gives `apps.code | setup install.tui ...`. The current-menu rows and the deeper rows now share one section. The PR says only \"with the divider following them\". Our TKDP rewrite (\"one divider separates the apps from all menu entries\") and the witness at menumodel-replay.test.mjs:1406 codify the new form. That is our reading, not the author's statement.","refs":[{"id":"shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml","kind":"file","line":705},{"id":"test/node/menumodel-replay.test.mjs","kind":"file","line":1406},{"id":"SW-REQ-260922-TKDP","kind":"requirement"}],"severity":"medium","title":"Question: is dropping the direct/deeper divider whenever an app matches intended?","verification":{"evidence":[],"method":"behavior hazard: settled only by a recorded test outcome","note":"A runtime-behavior question the package's static facts cannot settle; it needs a test. Suggested test: \"Divider placement with direct, deeper and app matches all present\".","status":"needs_test"}},{"claim":{"params":{"relatesTo":["shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml:rebuildDisplay"],"scenario":"root search 'e' with 200 installed apps: index of the first menu row in the result list"},"type":"behavior_hazard"},"detail":"Every matching app now precedes every menu row. In my own scratch run at d29af2a6 with synthetic apps that all match `e`, the first menu row moved from index 0 (base 58cd8018) to index 20 with 20 apps and to index 200 with 200 apps. The PR screenshots show one-app cases only.","refs":[{"id":"shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml","kind":"file","line":711},{"id":"SW-REQ-260922-TKDP","kind":"requirement"}],"severity":"low","title":"Question: with many installed apps, do short queries bury every