d":"SW-REQ-260922-4079","kind":"requirement"},{"id":"SW-REQ-260922-50RE","kind":"requirement"},{"id":"SW-REQ-260922-8CQ4","kind":"requirement"},{"id":"SW-REQ-260922-B757","kind":"requirement"},{"id":"SW-REQ-260922-DE93","kind":"requirement"},{"id":"SW-REQ-260922-NM45","kind":"requirement"},{"id":"SW-REQ-260922-Z48F","kind":"requirement"},{"id":"SYS-REQ-260922-P708","kind":"requirement"}],"severity":"info","title":"Obligation cells: 39 observed_pass, 34 not_linked; the live-session menu tests have observed outcomes","verification":{"evidence":[],"method":"untyped finding","note":"No typed claim: this finding is the author's judgement and is not checked against the package.","status":"unverifiable"}},{"detail":"review.effects is absent for this JS/QML change. The empty spec-gap list therefore proves nothing about uncodified connections (see the review.scope approximations). From reading the code: searchScore's only callers are the Menu.qml searchScore() wrapper, which feeds rebuildDisplay, plus test assertions. resolveRoute does not use it. These are facts from reading, not engine-verified facts.","refs":[{"id":"review.effects.approximations","kind":"check"},{"id":"shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml","kind":"file","line":711}],"severity":"info","title":"Change effects were not analyzed (effects_unavailable); uncodified connections cannot be detected","verification":{"evidence":[],"method":"untyped finding","note":"No typed claim: this finding is the author's judgement and is not checked against the package.","status":"unverifiable"}}],"packageDigest":"sha256:5b30180a8a1d0451d966893a0f5e4a15c660fbac1b321cb50296b0867f95465a","packageIdentity":"epkg-252cf4a20faac4cd9fd65ee53aa9e17231e5cb7f9ba04db1d1adaf34b2ed6019","riskAssessment":{"level":"medium","rationale":"The change deliberately reorders every menu search. Enter's target changes for many queries, including some where a menu entry matches the label exactly. It carries 4 unapproved compatibility changes, plus an inverted upstream assertion that no compat finding records. The configured differential does not exercise ranking. The engine rates risk low on gates and coverage. This assessment is advisory only."},"schemaVersion":"reqproof.review-annotation.v1","suggestedTests":[{"forClaim":10,"rationale":"Pins the maintainer's decision either way. Root 'system' with btop installed, and 'terminal' with Alacritty: assert which row is first.","refs":[{"id":"test/node/menumodel-replay.test.mjs","kind":"file","line":1425}],"title":"Exact-label menu entry vs keyword-only app"},{"forClaim":11,"rationale":"For root 'tu' with one matching app, assert the boundary count and position. This turns the divider change into a decided, pinned behaviour.","refs":[{"id":"test/node/menumodel-replay.test.mjs","kind":"file","line":1406}],"title":"Divider placement with direct, deeper and app matches all present"},{"forClaim":12,"rationale":"With 200 synthetic app rows, record the index of the first menu row for one-letter queries and assert a bound the maintainer accepts.","refs":[{"id":"shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml","kind":"file","line":711}],"title":"Burial at scale"},{"forClaim":13,"rationale":"Enumerate tiers x kinds x realistic depth/order and assert app max < menu min. It fails loudly if a tier >= 98 is added.","refs":[{"id":"shell/plugins/menu/MenuModel.js","kind":"file","line":377}],"title":"Tier-gap invariant property test"}],"summary":"**What the PR does.** Upstream #12223 (ax1g) ranks installed apps above menu entries in menu search. On the mirror it is commit f307af8a, identical to upstream head b74292ac. `searchScore` changes the app bias from -5 to -100 (MenuModel.js:377), so any matching app outranks any matching menu entry. `rebuildDisplay` pins matching app rows above the current menu's rows and re-derives the divider (Menu.qml:695-713). Upstream also adds a `vsc` test to menu-test.sh and inverts one assertion. Every later mirror commit is our proof work: spec text and witnesses, the #10340 test, citation re-points, two reviews, a KI note, trace re-reviews, and a tip trace review of the baseline's STK-REQ-260922-XTNR link.\n\n**Is the fix verified?** The changed decisions are covered: 0 uncovered lines or outcomes. The run ingested 57 results: 57 passed, 0 failed. I re-ran the node suites at d29af2a6: 30 passed, 1 skip (#10601 needs Qt). Base 58cd8018 vs head `rebuildDisplay`: for `vsc` VS Code now comes first; for `system` btop sits above the exact-label System menu.\n\n**Compatibility.** The 4 compat findings are unapproved, each a compat_change_unapproved disclosure that prevents ready. Two are test_diff changes and two are removed-behaviour items in the #10340 test helper. All four follow the PR's stated intent. The 28 compat_auditor_note disclosures are notes, not approvals; only a human reviewer approves. The differential ran 213 inputs with no difference, but its harness does not exercise ranking.\n\n**Questions for a human.** (1) Should a keyword-only app beat an exact-label menu entry? (2) Is dropping the direct/deeper divider when an app matches intended? (3) Can many apps bury menu entries?\n\n**Traceability.** SJ7P and TKDP were modified; 39 more are code_changed through file-level traces. The PR does not touch shell/services/AppSearch.js or SW-REQ-261003-C9GM: it reorders app rows, C9GM decides which apps exist. No spec-gap candidates; effects were not analyzed.\n\n**Not caused by this PR.** No check failed; 13 were skipped by configuration. Readiness is not_assessed. The next decision is human_judgement (compat_changes_unapproved), by a reviewer."}
